  THE LAYOUT IS WORTH REAL NAMING, ON BOTH AXES. Against its OWN
  no-index control the 2x2 grid buys +0.137 of `nearest` (6.0 SE), with
  BOTH axes contributing: F1 +0.126 and F2 +0.082. ctxfour's same contrast
  on vowel-corner words is +0.118.

  AND IT CORRECTS ctxfour's VERDICT AS WELL AS ITS LAYOUT. That run read
  its oracle at 0.279 against 0.250 and called it chance, while its own
  off arm sat at 0.161 -- so its oracle beat its control too. Both runs
  were scored against a null their own tables contradicted.
